  "rules": "Action Points:\n\nEach character begins an adventure with **3 Action Points (AP)**. These do **not refresh** and cannot normally be regained. AP represent the character’s inner reserve of **focus, resolve, and tactical brilliance** — the kind of instinct that flips the scene from disaster to legend.\n\nSpending AP:\n\nAt any moment, you may spend **1 Action Point** to:\n\n* **Gain Advantage**: You roll with edge, no matter what tags or odds say.\n* **Cancel a Failure**: Turn a failed roll into a *success with a cost*.\n* **Avoid a Consequence**: Dodge harm, exposure, or narrative fallout.\n* **Do the Impossible**: Pull off something daring, cinematic, and untagged — sliding under a trapdoor, mid-air grappling hook, bluffing your way past a kill team. You succeed *with style*.\n\n> \\[TIP]\n> Action Points are best spent when the scene demands momentum, not logic. Ask yourself: *Would this make a great moment?* If yes, spend.\n\nPush Yourself (Regain 1 AP):\n\nOnce per adventure, you may **Push Yourself** to regain 1 Action Point — but it comes at a cost. Choose one:\n\n* **Take a Serious Consequence** — injury, exposure, lost trust, or something broken.\n* **Burn a Tag** — a piece of gear or a trait is marked unusable for the rest of the adventure.\n* **Escalate the Situation** — make the scene worse: reinforcements arrive, the room floods, the item is a decoy, etc.\n\n> \\[CAUTION]\n> This isn’t a reset button — it’s a red flag to the fiction. Push when the moment feels *big*, and be ready for the fallout.",
  "locations": [
    {
      "name": "Starlight Transit Hub",
      "brief": "A decaying sky-train station straddling three closed borders, used by exiles, smugglers, and broken spies. Surveillance is rumored to be operated by a defunct agency — or something stranger.",
      "encounters": "Border agents, Disguised fugitives, Data couriers, Black market maps, Hidden rooms."
    },
    {
      "name": "The Drowned Embassy",
      "brief": "An underwater ruin off the coast, once a sealed Cold War diplomatic site, now claimed by silt and whispers. Pressure-locked vaults and flooded archives hide truths no nation ever admitted.",
      "encounters": "Vault drones, Salvage teams, Leaking documents, Pressure-traps, Bone-silent corridors."
    },
    {
      "name": "Calle Obscura",
      "brief": "A shadowy alley network in a forgotten quarter of the city, known for vanishing those who know too much. Stories say if you walk it right, the alleys change — and sometimes offer deals.",
      "encounters": "Informants, Double agents, Memory merchants, Traps, Wrong doors."
    },
    {
      "name": "Blacksite Theta-6",
      "brief": "A jungle-shrouded concrete installation erased from maps in 1984 — but still warm, still guarded. Its generators run on something not found in science books.",
      "encounters": "Rogue technicians, Burned files, Reality drift, Locked-down labs, False alarms."
    },
    {
      "name": "The Mirror Monastery",
      "brief": "A mountaintop retreat untouched by satellites, filled with fractured timelines and unreadable rituals. Its monks speak every language — including a few from the future.",
      "encounters": "Silent novices, Repeating events, Blinking icons, Forgotten visitors, Shattered mirrors."
    },
    {
      "name": "Volcano Platform K-9",
      "brief": "A defunct mining rig turned helicopter outpost, built on the lip of an unstable volcano. Part radio relay, part arms depot, part trap for whoever gets curious.",
      "encounters": "Storm pilots, Smuggled crates, Seismic tremors, Countdown timers, Betrayals in progress."
    }
  ],
  "seeds": [
    "A stolen artifact resurfaces at an auction in Marrakesh. Three bidders carry weapons, one carries a curse.",
    "A cargo plane crashes near a jungle outpost. The black box was removed before the authorities arrived.",
    "A diplomat’s briefcase goes missing during a summit. Inside: a map, a key, and a death list.",
    "Your contact in Istanbul is late. His last message: “Don’t trust the mirror.”",
    "A sealed Cold War vault opens for the first time. The contents were meant to never be found.",
    "An informant vanishes from a safehouse. Her notebook appears two weeks later — in a museum display.",
    "A masked figure steals a relic from a private train car. The train hasn’t stopped in over 40 hours.",
    "Your mentor is accused of grave robbing. The tomb in question wasn’t built yet.",
    "A scientist’s defection unravels when her escort turns up dead — and she turns up again in two places.",
    "A resistance leader requests extraction — from a city wiped off the map twenty years ago.",
    "A luxury cruise goes dark mid-ocean. The last transmission: “The stars are wrong.”",
    "Your safe deposit box has been emptied. The thief left behind your old ID and a countdown.",
    "A museum exhibit burns in Berlin. All artifacts but one were destroyed — and it's following you.",
    "A vault under the Vatican unseals during renovations. Inside: Soviet film reels, a dagger, and blood.",
    "A tech CEO disappears before a major keynote. His prototype device is broadcasting from deep underground.",
    "An old friend invites you to their wedding — at an abandoned excavation site.",
    "A flooded temple rises during a drought. Four expeditions enter; only one returns. They won't speak.",
    "You inherit a lockbox from a missing relative. Inside is a revolver, three passports, and a cassette tape.",
    "A war criminal fakes their death — then resurfaces as a cult leader in the Andes.",
    "A hotel fire reveals a hidden floor with no access points. Every room contains the same photo.",
    "An encrypted radio signal plays a forgotten anthem. It hasn’t broadcast since the embassy bombing in ’78.",
    "An illegal auction lists a live lot: the man who stole your identity.",
    "An underground fight ring offers a huge prize. The catch: the winner gets recruited by someone worse.",
    "A smuggler offers to trade an ancient relic for protection — but only if you meet them inside a quarantined zone.",
    "Your contact in Morocco offers information in exchange for a favor: bury a locked case in the desert.",
    "A militia group captures a photographer who snapped something inhuman in their territory.",
    "A billionaire funds a jungle excavation and disappears. The only clue: a bloodstained telegram.",
    "You’re asked to retrieve a downed spy drone. It landed inside a military exclusion zone — 50 years ago.",
    "A warzone refugee speaks a dead language — and describes events from before the city existed.",
    "An expedition lost in Siberia is found alive and unaged — but one of them is not who they were.",
    "A data broker in Panama claims to have a list of future events. Everyone wants it. Including you.",
    "Your handler gives you a package to deliver — and then shoots themselves. The package breathes.",
    "You’re hired to guard a transport crate. No one tells you where it’s going — only who’s following.",
    "A private island used for classified testing sends a distress call. The project was terminated. Supposedly.",
    "A fortune teller gives you an old coin. Three agencies try to kill you within the hour.",
    "A dig team in Sudan vanishes mid-call. When you arrive, the camp is gone — but the signal remains active."
  ],
